    "result_text": "All 5 test classes (11 tests) pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required that a created owner returns `displayName` formatted exactly as `'LastName, FirstName'` from the stored names. The `OwnerDto` returned by both `POST /api/owners` and `GET /api/owners/{ownerId}` is generated from the OpenAPI spec and mapped by MapStruct, so I made two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` response schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes the field). It's read-only, so it isn't part of the editable `OwnerFields` request payload.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` on `toOwnerDto(Owner)` with the expression `owner.getLastName() + \", \" + owner.getFirstName()`, computing the display name from the stored entity names. Because both the create responder (`RespondWithOwnerCreated`) and the fetch responder (`RespondWithOwner`) go through `toOwnerDto`, the field is populated consistently.\n\nThe new `Cp05Tests.coreComputesDisplayName` passes, and the full suite (11 tests) is green with no regressions.",
